Branches: SDD

Purpose:
  Branch naming and hierarchy standards for SDDRA projects.
  Enforces SDLC/STLC compliance and decision/task traceability.

Hierarchy:
  main:
    purpose: Production-ready code
    protection: required
    merge_to: stage

  stage:
    purpose: Staging integration
    protection: required
    merge_to: main

  test:
    purpose: Test environment
    protection: optional
    merge_to: stage

  MODUL/<module>:
    purpose: Module development branch
    parent: main
    example: MODUL/auth, MODUL/payment
    rule: one branch per bounded context module

  DEC/<id>:
    purpose: Decision implementation branch
    parent: MODUL/<module>
    example: DEC-001, DEC-002
    rule: one branch per approved decision
    rule: branch name MUST match decision ID exactly

  TASK/<id>:
    purpose: Task execution branch
    parent: DEC/<id>
    example: TASK-AUTH-001, TASK-PAYMENT-002
    rule: one branch per task
    rule: branch name MUST match task ID exactly

Rules:
  [B1]  Every commit MUST reference its linked DEC and TASK IDs.
  [B2]  Commit message format: <type>(<scope>): <subject> [DEC:<id>] [TASK:<id>]
  [B3]  MODUL branches are created during architecture phase.
  [B4]  DEC branches are created when decision is approved.
  [B5]  TASK branches are created from their linked DEC branch.
  [B6]  Branches MUST follow hierarchy: main -> stage -> test -> MODUL -> DEC -> TASK.
  [B7]  No direct commits to main, stage, or test — all via pull request.
  [B8]  TASK branch MUST be deleted after merge and archive.
  [B9]  DEC branch MUST be preserved for audit trail.
  [B10] MODUL branch persists for module lifetime.
  [B11] Branch protection rules apply at main and stage levels.
  [B12] Only changed files are tested — regression tests run only on unchanged code.

CommitFormat:
  types: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, test, chore, build, ci, perf, revert
  scopes: sdd, project, docs, chains, skills, prompts, commands, templates, patterns, workflows, decisions, gates, tests
  example: feat(auth): add login endpoint [DEC:DEC-001] [TASK:TASK-AUTH-001]

Navigation:
  SDLC: @sdlc.sdd
  STLC: @stlc.sdd
  Tasks: @../tasks/INDEX.sdd

State: +
